# Object-Oriented Patterns in TwinCAT3

## Rules

### Inheritance (`EXTENDS`)

- Call `SUPER^.Method()` when the parent implementation must run (InfoSys **SUPER**)
- Derived FB inherits base data/methods/properties; access follows PUBLIC/PROTECTED/PRIVATE (InfoSys **Inheritance principle**)
- Override when the base access modifier allows (not PRIVATE); method signature must match; `SUPER^` optional when replacing entirely

### Interfaces

- Define in `.TcIO` (`INTERFACE I_…`)
- Implement with `IMPLEMENTS`; all methods/properties required
- Call via interface variable after assigning a concrete instance
- Validity check: interface `<> 0` (not `__ISVALIDREF`) — InfoSys **Interface pointer / INTERFACE**, **__ISVALIDREF**

### Abstract FBs

- `FUNCTION_BLOCK ABSTRACT …` cannot be instantiated (InfoSys **ABSTRACT concept**)
- `METHOD ABSTRACT …` must be implemented by derived FBs (or the derived FB stays abstract)

### Properties

- PascalCase names, no type prefix
- XML: 3 GUIDs (Property + Get + Set) or 2 (read-only: Property + Get) — see `twincat3-xml`
- Omit Set for read-only

### `FB_init` dependency injection

- Implicitly called on download / Online Change (InfoSys **Operating cases**) — not only first create
- Guard DI with `IF bInCopyCode THEN RETURN; END_IF` (skip Online-Change copy path)
- Prefer `REFERENCE TO` for non-nullable deps; validate with `__ISVALIDREF` before use
- `FB_reinit` after Online Change copy (declaration/signature change) — not warm reset; `FB_exit` before instance teardown / new download (InfoSys **FB_reinit** / **Operating cases**)

